WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.140
A flat near the university.

2
00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:04.880
French has two ways to
finish that thought.

3
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.590
One: «un logement qui
soit proche de la fac».

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:10.680
Two: «un logement qui
est proche de la fac».

5
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.260
Same flat. Same distance.

6
00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:17.280
One small word apart, and they
don't tell the same story.

7
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.090
Now try the best film you've ever seen.

8
00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:22.910
Why does that call for
the special verb too?

9
00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.540
In this mission, you'll
build a two-part verb,

10
00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:28.590
piece by piece, in a colour-coded grid.

11
00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:31.770
Then you'll drag events
along a timeline in the lab:

12
00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:34.330
before, during or after?

13
00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.980
Your mission: find out
what the best film you've

14
00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:39.240
ever seen does to a French verb.
